Yes, this CMS Integration API RetryConfig is essentially the same pattern as the previous one. You can apply the same Reactor-based solution here.

I would make these changes:

1. Add doBeforeRetry()

Your current:

.filter(this::isRetryable)
.onRetryExhaustedThrow(...)

becomes:

.filter(this::isRetryable)
.doBeforeRetry(this::logRetry)
.onRetryExhaustedThrow((retryBackoffSpec, retrySignal) -> {
    logRetryExhausted(retrySignal);

    return new RuntimeException(
        "Retries exhausted for the request",
        retrySignal.failure()
    );
});

2. Remove logging from isRetryable()

Keep isRetryable() only for deciding whether to retry:

public boolean isRetryable(Throwable throwable) {
    if (throwable instanceof WebClientResponseException ex) {
        int statusCode = ex.getStatusCode().value();

        return statusCode >= 500 && statusCode < 600;
    }

    return true;
}

3. Add the retry logging methods

private void logRetry(RetrySignal retrySignal) {

    Throwable failure = retrySignal.failure();

    LogBuilder logBuilder = new LogBuilder()
            .withMessage("Retrying external API request")
            .withField(
                    "retryAttempt",
                    retrySignal.totalRetries() + 1
            )
            .withField(
                    "exceptionType",
                    failure.getClass().getSimpleName()
            )
            .withField(
                    "exceptionMessage",
                    failure.getMessage()
            );

    if (failure instanceof WebClientResponseException ex) {
        logBuilder.withField(
                "statusCode",
                ex.getStatusCode().value()
        );
    }

    log.error(logBuilder.toString(), failure);
}

private void logRetryExhausted(RetrySignal retrySignal) {

    Throwable failure = retrySignal.failure();

    LogBuilder logBuilder = new LogBuilder()
            .withMessage("Retries exhausted for the request")
            .withField(
                    "totalRetries",
                    retrySignal.totalRetries()
            )
            .withField(
                    "exceptionType",
                    failure.getClass().getSimpleName()
            )
            .withField(
                    "exceptionMessage",
                    failure.getMessage()
            );

    if (failure instanceof WebClientResponseException ex) {
        logBuilder.withField(
                "statusCode",
                ex.getStatusCode().value()
        );
    }

    log.error(logBuilder.toString(), failure);
}

You'll also need:

import reactor.util.retry.Retry.RetrySignal;

Final flow

API exception
     ↓
isRetryable()
     ↓
5xx / network exception → true
     ↓
doBeforeRetry()
     ↓
log exception + retryAttempt + status
     ↓
retry
     ↓
failure again
     ↓
doBeforeRetry()
     ↓
log retryAttempt 2
     ↓
...
     ↓
Retries exhausted
     ↓
log final exception

One thing I'd check before implementing

Since this is CMS Integration API, don't assume every RetryConfig usage needs the same exact message/component fields. First check the callers of:

createRetry(...)

If several CMS clients use this configuration, then this centralized change will cover all of them—which is preferable to adding logging individually in CMSApiService, CMSTokenService, CredentialServiceClient, OcmWebClient, etc.

Also, keep the existing retry behavior unchanged. The only intended behavior change here should be better retry observability.